 "conventions":
 "A joint angle is given only by its cosine and sine, because the chain reads an angle no other way (`dh_congr`, `fk_congr`); each `theta_cos_sin` entry is a pair of exact numerals. `carrier_pose` is the tower `0T_0` to `0T_6` of `Kinematics.carrierPose`, base frame first, each frame a rotation `R` and an origin `p` in base coordinates, and `carrier_matrix4` is the same seven frames as 4x4 homogeneous matrices, row-major, so rows are rows. `fk` is `Kinematics.fk`, the last entry of the tower. `wrist_center` is `Kinematics.wristCenter` of `fk`: the frame-4 origin, which `wrist_center_at_frame_one` additionally pins to the frame-1 origin in the cases that set it. `arm_rotation` and `wrist_rotation` are the two factors of `fk_R`. Geometry is named by the DH letters: `a2` is `Kinematics.Geometry.linkOne` and `d4` is `linkTwo`. Every numeral is an exact integer or \"num/den\" string, never a JSON number.",
